[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Slav Defence"]
[Variation "Czech Variation"]
[ECO "D17"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "light-bishop-out,c4-pawn-hold"]

1. d4 d5 { Claims a share of the centre and stops White playing e4 for free. } 2. c4 c6 { Defends d5 with a pawn, so Black can take on c4 later without giving up the centre. } 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 dxc4 { Takes the pawn now. White will win it back, but Black gets time to bring the c8 bishop out first. }
5. a4 ( 5. e3 b5 { With no pawn on a4, Black can hold the extra pawn. } 6. a4 b4 7. Na2 e6 ) 5... Bf5 { Develops the bishop outside the pawn chain before ...e6 shuts it in. It also stops White playing e4. [%cal Gf5e4] }
6. e3 ( 6. Ne5 { Hits c4 and f7 at once. } 6... Nbd7 { Challenges the knight on e5 and defends the knight on f6. } 7. Nxc4 Qc7 8. g3 e5 { Strikes at the centre before White finishes developing. } 9. dxe5 Nxe5 10. Bf4 Nfd7 )
6... e6 { Opens the bishop on f8 and guards d5 once more. } 7. Bxc4 Bb4 { Develops with a pin: the knight on c3 is pinned to the king on e1, so it cannot support e4 freely. [%cal Gb4c3] } 8. O-O Nbd7 9. Qe2 Bg6 { Moves the bishop out of reach of e4 and keeps it on the long diagonal. } 10. e4 O-O { Black castles and is fully developed. } 11. Bd3 *
